    <statement><p>Suppose <m>\displaystyle f(x) = h(g(x)k(x)).</m> If <m>g(1)=3,</m> <m>k(1)=0,</m> <m>h(1)=-6,</m> <m>g'(1)=8,</m> <m>k'(1)=-7,</m> <m>h'(1)=7,</m> and <m>h'(0)=2,</m> find <m>f'(1).</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>f'(1) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 3\cdot \left(-7\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
